### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Subscribe — reaction_added. config.channel_id scopes to one channel, config.message_ts scopes to
### reactions on ONE specific message (item.ts — always present on this event, safe to filter on, unlike
### newMessage's thread_ts). Omit both for "every reaction everywhere". No thread_ts here — a reaction_added
### event only carries the reacted-to message's own ts, not its parent thread_ts if it's itself a thread
### reply, so per-thread scoping isn't derivable without an extra conversations.replies lookup.
### ----------------------------------------------------
POST {{base_url}}/triggers/slack/reaction_added/subscribe
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "connection_id": "{{slack_connection_id}}",
  "webhook_url": "https://webhook.site/your-unique-url-here",
  "config": { "channel_id": "{{slack_channel}}" },
  "extra_metadata": { "notes": "for the #support-eu channel" }
}

