### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Subscribe — file_shared, scoped to one channel. Needs the files:read bot EVENT scope (distinct from
### files:write, which upload_file the ACTION uses) — see .env.example. Slack's file_shared event only
### carries IDs (file_id/channel_id/user_id), not the filename/title — call files.info with file_id if you
### need those (no files.info action exists in this app yet).
### ----------------------------------------------------
POST {{base_url}}/triggers/slack/file_shared/subscribe
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "connection_id": "{{slack_connection_id}}",
  "webhook_url": "https://webhook.site/your-unique-url-here",
  "config": { "channel_id": "{{slack_channel}}" },
  "extra_metadata": { "notes": "for the #support-eu channel" }
}

### ----------------------------------------------------
### 🔧 Slack's own Events API delivery endpoint — this is what Slack calls, not something a client calls
### directly. Included here for reference/local testing (e.g. replaying a captured payload with curl).
### First-time setup: Slack sends a `url_verification` challenge here and expects it echoed back.
### ----------------------------------------------------
POST {{base_url}}/webhooks/slack/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "url_verification",
  "challenge": "test-challenge-token"
}

# ============================================================================
# ADMIN — read-only inspection, filter by app in the response yourself (no per-app query param)
# ============================================================================

### 🔧 Admin — users
GET {{base_url}}/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_access_token}}

### 🔧 Admin — trigger instances
GET {{base_url}}/admin/triggers
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_access_token}}

# ============================================================================
# LISTEN TO EVERYTHING THIS USER HAS TRIGGERED — two separate concerns, both needed together
# ============================================================================
#
# 1) SUBSCRIBE to every trigger you want live events for. There is no bulk "subscribe to all triggers"
#    endpoint — POST /triggers/:app/:trigger/subscribe is per trigger key, same as every individual
#    subscribe call above. To cover every Gmail/Slack trigger that exists right now: 4 Gmail (new_email,
#    new_sent_email, new_starred_email, new_draft — all poll-mode, need worker.ts running) + 8 Slack
#    (new_message, message_edited, message_deleted, reaction_added, reaction_removed, user_joined_channel,
#    channel_created, file_shared — all webhook-mode, delivered via /webhooks/slack/events, see GET
#    /triggers below for the live/authoritative list instead of hand-counting). Point every subscribe call
#    at the SAME webhook_url and every fired event — across every app/trigger you subscribed to — lands on
#    that one URL, tagged with its own `type` (e.g. "gmail.new_email" / "slack.reaction_added") in the
#    envelope so your receiver can tell them apart. No per-instance filter (config) on any of them = fires
#    for everything that trigger can see, not scoped to one channel/thread/message.
#
### 🔧 List every real trigger that exists, across every app — the authoritative source for step 1 above,
### not this file's hand-maintained comment.
GET {{base_url}}/triggers
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
#
# 2) READ what's already fired — GET /triggers/logs (used throughout this file per-instance via
#    GET /triggers/instances/:id/logs) also has a NOT-scoped-to-one-instance form: every log row across
#    EVERY trigger this user has ever subscribed to, Gmail and Slack together, one unified list. Quiet
#    "checked, found nothing" poll rows are hidden by default (Gmail only — Slack is webhook-mode, it has
#    no poll-attempt rows at all); `data_found`/`data_sendable` on each row tell you "was this a real event"
#    and "did delivery to webhook_url actually succeed" without needing to parse `status`/`error` yourself.
#
### 🔧 Every event this user has ever had fire, across every app/trigger — most recent first, default
### limit 20, with_payload=true (each row inlines the exact envelope delivered, no second call needed).
GET {{base_url}}/triggers/logs?user_id={{user_id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
#
### 🔧 Same thing, narrowed to just this app (drop &app= to see Gmail+Slack together again)
GET {{base_url}}/triggers/logs?user_id={{user_id}}&app=slack
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
#
### 🔧 Include the normally-hidden quiet poll rows too (only meaningful for Gmail's poll-mode triggers —
### confirms the scheduler is actually ticking, separate from "did anything real happen")
GET {{base_url}}/triggers/logs?user_id={{user_id}}&include_empty_polls=true
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### 🔧 Admin — action/trigger call log
GET {{base_url}}/admin/logs?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{admin_access_token}}
